This project is intended to translate and extend ideas and implementation
behavior from the R packages gamlss and gamlss.dist by Mikis Stasinopoulos,
Robert Rigby, and contributors. Those packages are distributed under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or version 3.

TorchGAMLSS is not affiliated with or endorsed by the original authors.

Formula parsing and categorical encoding use Formulaic by Matthew Wardrop,
distributed under the MIT License. TorchGAMLSS adds its own GAMLSS-specific
handling for pb() and offset() terms.

The Normal and Gamma family parity implementations and fixtures are derived
from and tested against gamlss.dist 6.1-1, in particular R/NO.r and R/GA.R,
and gamlss 5.5-0. Both source packages are distributed by CRAN under GPL-2 or
GPL-3.

The Poisson, negative-binomial type I, and Beta implementations and fixtures
are derived from and tested against the PO, NBI, and BE family definitions in
gamlss.dist 6.1-1. The shared starting-value behavior follows the corresponding
family initialization expressions. These translations remain under
GPL-3.0-only.

The linear RS fitting implementation is translated from the algorithm in
gamlss 5.5-0, R/gamlss-5.R, by Mikis Stasinopoulos, Robert Rigby, and
contributors. The translated implementation remains under GPL-3.0-only.

Full-Hessian covariance and Wald inference behavior follows vcov.gamlss(),
gen.likelihood(), and summary.gamlss() in gamlss 5.5-0. The translated
behavior remains under GPL-3.0-only.

Likelihood diagnostics and model-selection criteria follow logLik.gamlss(),
deviance.gamlss(), GAIC.gamlss(), and the fitted degrees-of-freedom conventions
in gamlss 5.5-0. Quantile residual behavior follows residuals.gamlss(), the
family rqres definitions, and the shared rqres() helper in gamlss.dist 6.1-1.
The translated behavior remains under GPL-3.0-only.

The additive backfitting and P-spline implementation, including fixed, ML,
target-EDF, GAIC, and GCV smoothing-parameter selection, is translated from
gamlss 5.5-0, in particular R/add.r and R/pb.R. The latter credits work by
Mikis Stasinopoulos, Robert Rigby, Paul Eilers, and Simon Wood. The translated
implementation remains under GPL-3.0-only.
